    "body": "## User-visible defect\nExisting iPhone saves resumed directly into the old unrestricted world. The Stage 7.1 controller returned `claimed: false` whenever its dedicated snapshot key did not yet exist, so pre-existing saves bypassed the new first causal experience entirely.\n\n## Fix\n- treat a started legacy save without `AsyncScene_first_experience_v1` as a one-time migration into the Stage 7 first experience\n- preserve the completed-scenario gate so users who already settled the world advance are not replayed\n- record `legacy_resume_migration` telemetry\n- bump the Stage 7 controller cache-buster from `20260805a` to `20260805b` so Safari fetches the fixed script\n- add focused regression assertions that the legacy bypass condition cannot return\n\n## Exact scope\n1. `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-stage7-first-experience.js`\n2. `docs/ui/ui-stage7-first-experience.js`\n3. `AsyncScene/Web/index.html`\n4. `docs/index.html`\n5. `tools/test_stage7_first_causal_vertical_slice.py`\n\n## Validation\n- Stage 7.1 focused regression PASS\n- Stage 7 essence modal regression PASS\n- Stage 7 pre-start overlay regression PASS\n- Step 9 forbidden state-access harness PASS\n- Stage 6 profile-bootstrap findings PASS\n- Node syntax PASS for both controller mirrors\n- JS and index mirror parity PASS\n- `git diff --check` PASS\n- final branch diff contains exactly five files",
